  "source": "experiments/20260921_h_soft_anchor_gate_recalibrated_noisefloor_replay.json",
  "notes": "For each K' in 1..K_MAX, 'mean_empirical_subset_mean_variance' is the actual variance of the mean across all C(5, K') same-size subsets of each group's 5 already-collected judge draws, averaged across groups. 'mean_theoretical_variance_over_k' is the naive i.i.d. prediction (each group's own 5-draw sample variance / K'), averaged the same way. A ratio near 1.0 at every K' supports plain i.i.d. scaling (ruverbench2606's diminishing returns is then just ordinary 1/K variance scaling, nothing repo-specific). A ratio that grows with K means repeats help less than naively assumed (positively correlated per-group judge draws); a ratio below 1.0 would mean repeats help MORE than naively assumed. This is a K_MAX=5-per-group check (34 groups) -- modest power, same spirit as cycles 19-22's own low-power caveats; report honestly.",
  "synthetic_control_check": {
    "purpose": "Discovered during ANALYZE_RESULTS: the real-run empirical_over_theoretical_ratio curve (1.0, 0.667, 0.444, 0.25 at K=1..4) looked like evidence of positive correlation between repeated judge calls on the same input. This control reruns the IDENTICAL analysis method (exhaustive combinatorial subset-mean variance over C(5,k) subsets of a FIXED 5-draw sample) on synthetic data drawn from a true i.i.d. Gaussian(50, 10) generator (random.seed(42), 34 groups x 5 draws each) with NO correlation whatsoever by construction.",
    "result": {
      "1": {
        "mean_empirical_subset_mean_variance": 88.10831879913918,
        "mean_theoretical_variance_over_k": 88.10831879913918,
        "empirical_over_theoretical_ratio": 1.0
      },
      "2": {
        "mean_empirical_subset_mean_variance": 29.36943959971306,
        "mean_theoretical_variance_over_k": 44.05415939956959,
        "empirical_over_theoretical_ratio": 0.6666666666666666
      },
      "3": {
        "mean_empirical_subset_mean_variance": 13.05308426653914,
        "mean_theoretical_variance_over_k": 29.36943959971306,
        "empirical_over_theoretical_ratio": 0.4444444444444445
      },
      "4": {
        "mean_empirical_subset_mean_variance": 5.506769924946201,
        "mean_theoretical_variance_over_k": 22.027079699784796,
        "empirical_over_theoretical_ratio": 0.25000000000000006
      },
      "5": {
        "mean_empirical_subset_mean_variance": null,
        "mean_theoretical_variance_over_k": 17.62166375982784,
        "empirical_over_theoretical_ratio": null
