    "conclusion": "The synthetic (true-iid, zero-correlation) curve is numerically IDENTICAL (1.0, 0.667, 0.444, 0.25) to the real experiment curve. This proves the empirical_over_theoretical_ratio shrinking below 1.0 as K grows is a deterministic artifact of exhaustively enumerating subsets WITHOUT replacement from a small FIXED finite sample (classic finite-population-correction effect), not evidence about whether this repos actual judge calls are positively or negatively correlated. The experiment as designed cannot distinguish real judge-call correlation from this guaranteed combinatorial effect -- treat the diminishing_returns_curve comparison above as INVALID for its intended purpose, per PLAYBOOK.md ANALYZE_RESULTS confound-disclosure rule."
